HSL Color Format:

# Hue (0-360): Position on the color wheel
# 0 = Red
# 30 = Orange
# 60 = Yellow
# 120 = Green
# 180 = Cyan
# 210 = Light Blue
# 240 = Blue
# 270 = Purple
# 300 = Pink
# 330 = Magenta
# Saturation (0-100): How vivid/intense the color is
# 0 = Gray (no color)
# 50 = Moderate
# 100 = Fully saturated (most vivid)
# Lightness (0-100): How bright the color is
# 0 = Black
# 25 = Dark
# 50 = Medium
# 75 = Light
# 100 = White
# Common brand colors:

# Red: Hue 0, Saturation 70-80, Lightness 45-55
# Orange: Hue 30, Saturation 80-90, Lightness 50-55
# Yellow: Hue 45-50, Saturation 90-100, Lightness 50-55
# Green: Hue 120-140, Saturation 60-70, Lightness 40-50
# Blue: Hue 210-240, Saturation 70-90, Lightness 40-50
# Purple: Hue 270-290, Saturation 60-80, Lightness 45-55
# Pink: Hue 330-350, Saturation 70-85, Lightness 55-65